WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.909
I think it's important not to celebrate prematurely.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:08.680
The student loan debt forgiveness that has
been announced by Joe Biden.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:15.349
And the reason I say that is that it is looking
slightly more plausible that that student

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:17.310
loan debt forgiveness could end up blocked.

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.250
Now, earlier in the week, we discussed this
on the bonus show.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.160
And when we talked about it on the bonus show.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.500
The bonus show where you want to make money
and everybody else that makes money to fund

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.670
themselves is bad.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.839
Among other things, one of the things that
came up is that disgusting.

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:34.550
Republican Senator Ted Cruz is working on
blocking it.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:38.629
And one of the things that came up in our
discussion about Ted Cruz is that even Ted

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:43.270
Cruz was admitting he isn't totally clear
on who could bring a lawsuit.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:51.090
Could it be a taxpayer who says, hey, 20 $100
supposedly of my tax money is being used to

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.760
pay off someone's student loans or to forgive
someone's student loans, and that hurts me.

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.140
So I'm filing a lawsuit.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.550
Would a random taxpayer have standing?

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:04.350
What about someone who just is outside of
the income range for forgiveness?

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:09.580
Like if you make 126,000 instead of $125,000,
it's not clear.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:15.259
But increasingly, it seems as though it is
at least plausible that the plan could be

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:16.299
blocked.

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:20.030
Arizona's Republican attorney general said
he and others are looking at

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:25.350
bringing a legal challenge to Joe Biden's
plan for the cancelation of student debt.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:30.640
If we can bring a challenge, we will bring
a challenge, he said to CNBC in an interview

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:32.210
on Tuesday.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:37.140
The state's Republican attorney general said
he and others are looking to bring a challenge

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:43.479
and GOP attorneys attorneys general from Missouri
and Texas, as well as Ted Cruz, who I already

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:50.860
mentioned all are figuring out how might we
be able to block Joe Biden's plan.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:54.990
And this is causing understandable anxiety
for the tens of millions that stand to benefit

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.210
from this plan.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:02.250
Now, as CNBC writes, a drawn out legal challenge
would threaten to throw the fate of an estimated

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:07.070
43 million people's debts into limbo for the
foreseeable future.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:11.050
And the issue could make its way to the Supreme
Court.

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:13.130
Laurence Tribe, Harvard law professor, wrote.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.720
The uncertainty for borrowers in the

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.440
meantime is considerable.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.440
No lawsuits have yet been filed.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.530
But it looks like they want to do it sooner
than later.

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.850
So there's a couple of different things here
that I think are important.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:34.250
One is, yes, it is completely plausible at
this point, based on all of the legal opinions

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:39.440
I've read, it is plausible that this could
be tied up for years.

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:46.850
Now, whether ultimately it will be found to
be within Joe Biden's purview and something

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:50.400
he can do and something that's legal and something
that can be done, I don't know.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.590
But if it gets tied up for years before any
forgiveness is done, that's still going to

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.950
be very bad for 43 million borrowers.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:56.950
That's number one.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.060
Number two, this also could backfire on Republicans.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:07.280
We have seen for months now the chances for
Democrats in the House and Senate tick up

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.280
and up and

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:09.280
up slowly.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.920
Yes, but they have ticked up and up and up.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.240
And part of that is on the backs of the overturning
of Roe v Wade, much too much celebrated by

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.960
many Republican officials, not popular with
the American public.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:24.170
Part of it has been Republican inaction on
gun safety.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:29.200
And we know from polling that this level,
this degree of student loan debt forgiveness

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.080
that has been offered is quite popular with
the American people.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:38.230
So while indeed it is something Republicans
might be able to hold up, it also appears

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:42.980
to be something that Republicans should be
cautious about holding up, because it does

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:47.490
not seem as though the the American people
actually want it stopped.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:51.360
But at this point, it is getting enough momentum
behind it.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:55.510
The block, the forgiveness movement that it
would be weird not to mention the fact that

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.510
it is not a

00:03:56.510 --> 00:05:15.840
complete and total foregone conclusion.

